        "reasons": "NO_PLAN with a MARKET_VOLUME decisive gap is right. Recomputed: $400,000 / $500 = 800 purchases needed. The card's buyerVolume (EVIDENCE) counts 380 association dealerships, each buying at most one list a month, so in a 14-day window at most 380 purchases = $190,000 gross ($186,200 net of the $10 direct cost) even at 100% conversion; at the measured 22/110 = 20% conversion, 76 deals = $38,000. Even if every remaining unknown were resolved favourably this population cannot fit the target, so it is a constraint rather than missing evidence. Price is this buyer population's own paid records, settlement (5 days) and zero exposure fit, so no other link is decisive.",
